      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, and many references use 2,000 mg/day. Doses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals**, or another dose.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
